// Dialog :
"P462114930" "As you're counting the money you stole and thinking of all the influence it will get you, you hear the voice of Radio Free Opportunity break in to whatever the radio was tuned to before: <br><br>'It's Radio-RADIO-RADIOOOOO Free Opportunity, where evil always wins, even when good plays it smart. The big news today is {VillainName}'s daring theft from Wyvern. With their operating budget stolen, no one knows what they're going to do. Now I wonder where {VillainName} found out about that little job? Oh, yeah! I remember! It was right here on Radio Free Opportunity.'"
// RandomFameString :
"P1584871205" "I've heard that the Wyvern vigilantes are really hurting for cash. Wonder if they'll start robbing places?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - BrokerMission4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - WitchNotes 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2661448405" "The Sea Witch's notes"
// DetailString :
"P1930097539" "These notes detail the Sea Witch's findings during her month-long campaign against the shipping out of Dockside. According to these notes, Mr. Bocor has his fingers into the Family's Superadine trade, Arachnos' experiments with the ghosts, and every other major operation going on in Port Oakes. He even has ties to several of the Red Hands themselves."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2517396933" "Have you heard of the heroine who styles herself the Sea Witch? She has been causing a lot of trouble with the shipping out of Dockside lately, by convincing the Red Hands and Night Haunts to attack the vessels. And I have certain vested interests in those vessels. Now, we could battle the ghosts themselves; in fact, I have many spells for just that purpose. But I always believe it's better to go after the source. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>I need you to defeat the Sea Witch.</a> I have tracked her to a lair in Dockside. Make sure she knows that Mr. Bocor is watching her."
// AcceptString :
"P995321884" "Defeat the Sea Witch."
// SendOffString :
"P2097269101" "That's right, I said 'heroine,' not 'vigilante.' We have no need for illusions or euphemisms between us, {VillainName}. There are those who fight consistently for the side of right, and they are heroes. And then there are those like us, who know how to turn the powers of the world to our advantage. Personally, I would rather be the latter any day."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P999614479" "Defeat the Sea Witch"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3752683152" "The Sea Witch must know the crushing weight of your fist."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P1741313550" "This seaside cave smells of the ocean's salt."

